Requirement Analysis – Identify the project requirements, features, and user needs.
Environment Setup – Install Python, FastAPI, Streamlit, Gemini API libraries, and other required packages.
Backend Development – Develop the backend using FastAPI to handle API requests and application logic.
AI Integration – Integrate the Google Gemini API to provide AI-powered functionality.
Frontend Development – Create the user interface using Streamlit.
Document Processing – Use Python libraries such as python-docx, FPDF, and Pillow for document and file processing.
Testing – Test the application to identify and fix errors and ensure that all features work correctly.
Integration – Connect the frontend, backend, and Gemini AI components into a complete application.
Final Deployment – Run and deploy the completed application for users.
Maintenance – Monitor the application and make improvements or fixes when required.
